    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contact Details (e.g. Tox ID or email)\n\n_No response_\n\n### Feature Description\n\nIf I sign in to qTox (linux) after having received many messages while offline, a new message notification seems to appear for each message. This can cause dozens of small notification boxes to show at the same time for any specific user, along with all of their messages. I suggest that when these situations occur, it group them together to show a single message, something like showing their name/profile picture but for the message say something like \"N new messages\". Or perhaps showing the latest message along with text like \"N additional message(s)\".\n\nThere may be other situations this could occur besides when first signing in as well, for example if someone isn't online or connected for you but still tries to send you messages, then the connection completes and all of the messages go through at once - although you may have been online the whole time, I'd imagine you'd still get all of the same kind of notifications at once.\n\nI'm also not sure if there is any special handling for whether or not qTox knows if you're 'away' from the client and whether or not it attempts to continue to display these notifications until you interact with the client, but if there is that may be another situation where it could benefit from grouped handling - ie, when additional messages from the same user are detected, disposing/not creating the specific message notifications but instead appending a grouped counter notification.\n\n### Contribution\n\n- [ ] I would like to contribute to this feature",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
