            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I'm all for grouping the notifications. I ungrouped them while implementing notification categories. The previous grouping implementation only ever permitted one notification for all Tox activity, which isn't really compatible with categorizing individual activity.\r\n\r\nIf we want to use more than one notification (to allow for categories), but not one notification for every activity such that it \"floods\", I have some ideas.\r\n\r\nPerhaps the easiest solution would be to modify the old implementation. Set the [\"replaces id\"](https://specifications.freedesktop.org/notification-spec/latest/basic-design.html) of each notification based on category. This way, we get only a handful of notifications at once, tops. It would look something like this: \"4 messages from 2 friends\", \"Incoming call from friendname\", \"3 File transfers from 2 friends\".\r\n\r\nIf we wanted to take that idea even further, we could additionally group based on contact, displaying each message from a in full in one notification, with one notification per contact. The Replaces ID could be derived from the contact number concatenated to the notification type (text, call, file transfer). The trouble would be that each time it replaces the notification, it needs to statefully have all of the messages it wants to show. To my knowledge, you can't simply append to a notification once it has been dispatched. The XMPP client Dino has this behavior, so it's not impossible.",
